# UI mockups before appreciable changes

When changing UI in this project:

## Mock up first

Show a mockup (image, Storybook-only sketch, or short visual note the user can open) **before** implementing when the change is:

- A **whole new component** or screen
- A **wholesale replacement** of an existing layout/flow (new structure, not the same chrome with tweaks)
- A clearly new interaction pattern managers/drivers will need to relearn

Get a quick OK on the mockup, then implement.

## Skip mockups

Do **not** block on mockups for:

- Copy/label fixes, icon swaps, spacing/color tweaks
- Bug fixes that keep the same structure
- Small shifts (e.g. humanizing button text, fixing a wrong Autocomplete label, adding a section header)

If unsure, prefer a 30-second sketch over shipping a surprise redesign.
